(a) All new construction in the Houston special flood hazard areas, or substantial improvement of any existing structure in special flood hazard areas, shall be performed to keep the structure reasonably safe from flooding and in accordance with the following standards:

(1) Improvements shall be designed or modified to adequately anchor them to prevent flotation, collapse, or lateral movement of the structure in the presence of floodwaters;

(2) Improvements shall be constructed by methods and practices to minimize flood damage;

(3) Improvements shall be constructed with materials and equipment resistant to flood damage;

(4) Electrical, heating, ventilation, plumbing, and air conditioning equipment and other service facilities shall be designed and located above minimum flood protection elevation to prevent water from entering or accumulating within the components during conditions of flooding;

(5) Water supply systems shall be designed to prevent or eliminate infiltration of floodwaters into the system;

(6) Sanitary sewer systems shall be designed to prevent or eliminate infiltration of floodwaters into the structure's systems and discharge of sewage into floodwaters;

(7) On-site disposal systems, including but not limited to sewage treatment plants and septic tank systems located on the site of the structure, shall be located to prevent impairment of the function of those systems in the presence of floodwaters and to prevent contamination of floodwaters from those systems during flooding; and

