(a) The owner of a contributing structure located within an historic district or of a protected landmark shall not permit the contributing structure or protected landmark to fall into a serious state of disrepair so as to result in the deterioration of any exterior architectural feature.

This section applies to a structure regardless of whether it is occupied or vacant. An owner shall prevent or repair the following when necessary:

